{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the media:\n- Card_Art_Green: solid green (#3DD68C-ish) with white squiggle top-left, orange/red circle rings bottom-left, dark lightning arrow bottom-right. Text on green card: white will contrast well; the number **** 3447 in white SemiBold.\n- Card_Art_Pink: pink with white/green rings, purple arrow.\n- Card_Art_Purple: light purple (#BFB7FD-ish) with white/orange rings, pink arrow.\n- Logos: colorful brand icons 40×40.\n- Crypto: dark circle Solana, orange Bitcoin circle, purple Ethereum circle.\n- Flag_USA, Flag_Indonesia (red/white), Avatar_Neutral (light lavender circle with person icon).\n- Icons: outline style, ink strokes, 24×24.\n\nCard art text placement: I'll put holder name + number + expiry in white on the green card. For pink and purple cards in profile, also white text might work on pink (#F9B8D0?) — white on pink is low contrast; dark ink might be better for pink. Let me decide: green card → white text; pink card → ink text (#151521); purple card → ink? On #BFB7FD purple, white is okay-ish, ink better. Profile mini cards: just show art thumbnails without text (numbers shown in row text next to art). Good — avoids contrast issues.\n\nNow let me start building. First call: setup — create 11 empty frames named exactly, plus my reusable components on the workspace page. Then subsequent calls fill content.\n\nLet me define the palette & metrics precisely:\n\n```\nCOLORS:\nink      #151521  (0.0824, 0.0824, 0.1294)\nink80    #3D3B49\nsec      #6B6880  secondary text\nmuted    #A5A3B0\nfaint    #C9C7D3\nborder   #E9E7F2\nbg       #F6F5FA\ncard     #FFFFFF\nchip     #EFEDF8\nprimary  #BFB7FD\ndeep     #7C68EE\ndeepSoft #EDEAFD (light lavender for selected bg / icon circles alt)\nsuccess  #16A34A\nerror    #F04438\nwarning  #F59E0B\nwhite    #FFFFFF\n```\n\nFonts: PJS Regular 400, Medium 500, SemiBold 600. Note: font style names in Figma for Plus Jakarta Sans: \"Regular\", \"Medium\", \"SemiBold\"? The gotcha note says Inter is \"Semi Bold\". For Plus Jakarta Sans, Google font — in Figma it's \"SemiBold\" (one word) I believe. I'll verify with listAvailableFontsAsync filtered.\n\nType scale:\n- display: SemiBold 34 (balance)\n- h1: SemiBold 28 (Sign up title)\n- h2: SemiBold 22\n- h3: SemiBold 18 (screen titles, greeting)\n- body-sb: SemiBold 15 (card amounts)\n- body: Medium 15\n- body-r: Regular 15\n- label: Medium 14\n- small: Medium 13\n- small-r: Regular 13\n- caption: Medium 12\n- caption-r: Regular 12\n- micro: Regular 11\n- micro-m: Medium 11\n- tiny: Regular 10\n\nSpacing: 20 side padding (16 for dense), 12/16 section gaps.\n\nNow the helper library (pasted in each call):\n\n```js\nconst F = 'Plus Jakarta Sans';\nconst C = { ink:'#151521', ink80:'#3D3B49', sec:'#6B6880', muted:'#A5A3B0', border:'#E9E7F2', bg:'#F6F5FA', card:'#FFFFFF', chip:'#EFEDF8', primary:'#BFB7FD', deep:'#7C68EE', deepSoft:'#EDEAFD', success:'#16A34A', error:'#F04438', warning:'#F59E0B', white:'#FFFFFF', green:'#3DD68C' };\nfunction hx(h){h=h.replace('#','');return {r:parseInt(h.slice(0,2),16)/255,g:parseInt(h.slice(2,4),16)/255,b:parseInt(h.slice(4,6),16)/255};}\nfunction S(h,o){return {type:'SOLID',color:hx(h),opacity:o===undefined?1:o};}\nasync function loadFonts(){for(const s of ['Regular','Medium','SemiBold'])await figma.loadFontAsync({family:F,style:s});}\nfunction T(parent,chars,o){o=o||{};const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:F,style:o.st||'Medium'};t.fontSize=o.s||14;t.characters=chars;t.fills=[S(o.c||C.ink)];if(o.lh)t.lineHeight={px:o.lh};if(o.ls!==undefined)t.letterSpacing={px:o.ls};if(o.w){t.textAutoResize='NONE';t.resize(o.w,o.h||t.height);}else t.textAutoResize='WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT';if(o.a)t.textAlignHorizontal=o.a;if(o.x!==undefined)t.x=o.x;if(o.y!==undefined)t.y=o.y;parent.appendChild(t);return t;}\nfunction R(parent,o){const r=figma.createRectangle();r.resize(o.w,o.h);r.fills=o.f?[S(o.f,o.o)]:[];if(o.r!==undefined)r.cornerRadius=o.r;if(o.x!==undefined)r.x=o.x;if(o.y!==undefined)r.y=o.y;if(o.stroke){r.strokes=[S(o.stroke)];r.strokeWeight=o.sw||1;}if(o.dash)r.dashPattern=[4,4];parent.appendChild(r);return r;}\nfunction FR(parent,o){const f=figma.createFrame();f.resize(o.w,o.h);f.x=o.x||0;f.y=o.y||0;f.fills=o.f?[S(o.f,o.o)]:[];if(o.r!==undefined)f.cornerRadius=o.r;if(o.stroke){f.strokes=[S(o.stroke)];f.strokeWeight=o.sw||1;}if(o.dash)f.dashPattern=[4,4];if(o.effects)f.effects=o.effects;if(o.clip!==undefined)f.clipsContent=o.clip;f.name=o.name||'Frame';parent.appendChild(f);return f;}\nfunction ELL(parent,o){const e=figma.createEllipse();e.resize(o.w,o.h);e.x=o.x;e.y=o.y;e.fills=o.f?[S(o.f,o.o)]:[];if(o.stroke){e.strokes=[S(o.stroke)];e.strokeWeight=o.sw||1;}if(o.arc)e.arcData=o.arc;parent.appendChild(e);return e;}\nfunction icon(id,parent,x,y,size,tint){return figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id).then(c=>{const i=c.createInstance();i.resize(size,size);i.x=x;i.y=y;if(tint)tintIcon(i,tint);parent.appendChild(i);return i;});}\nfunction tintIcon(node,hex){const paint=S(hex);for(const ch of node.findAll(()=>true)){if('strokes'in ch&&ch.strokes&&ch.strokes.length>0)ch.strokes=[paint];if('fills'in ch&&ch.fills&&ch.fills.length>0&&ch.type!=='TEXT')ch.fills=[paint];}}\n```\n\nWait — tintIcon with findAll on instance: findAll works on instances and returns nodes (overridable). But careful: setting fills on vectors that have fills AND strokes. Icons are stroke-based; some may have fill parts (e.g., verified badge has green fill + white check; bitcoin logo has fills). tintIcon only used on mono icons.\n\nMedia component IDs:\n- Logos: Adobe_XD 2:24, Netflix 2:25, Line 2:26, PayPal 2:27, DANA 2:28, Google_Play 2:29, Shopee 2:30, Apple 2:31, Spotify 2:32\n- Crypto: Solana 2:33, Bitcoin 2:34, Ethereum 2:35\n- Cards: Green 2:36, Pink 2:37, Purple 2:38\n- Flag_USA 2:63, Flag_Indonesia 2:62, Avatar_Neutral 2:65\n- Icons: Home 2:2, Analytics 2:3, Cards 2:4, Profile 2:5, Bell 2:6, Message 2:7, Back 2:8, ArrowUpRight 2:9, Plus 2:10, Edit 2:11, Delete 2:12, Send 2:13, Receive 2:14, Search 2:15, Filter 2:16, ChevronDown 2:17, MoreH 2:18, MoreV 2:19, Comment 2:20, Like 2:21, Dislike 2:22, Verified 2:23\n- Button comp 3:52, TextField comp 3:71, StatusBar 6:110, HomeIndicator 6:122\n\nHelper for media instance:\n```js\nasync function media(id,parent,x,y,w,h){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const i=c.createInstance();if(h){i.resize(w,h);}else{i.resize(w,w);}i.x=x;i.y=y;parent.appendChild(i);return i;}\n```\n\nScreen scaffold:\n```js\nfunction screen(name,x,bg){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.resize(375,812);f.x=x;f.y=0;f.fills=[S(bg)];f.clipsContent=true;figma.currentPage.appendChild(f);return f;}\n```\n\nStatus bar + home indicator per screen:\n```js\nasync function shell(f,transparent){const sb=await media('6:110',f,0,0,375,44);if(transparent)sb.fills=[];const hi=await media('6:122',f,0,778,375,34);if(transparent)hi.fills=[];}\n```\n\nHmm, media() is async (getNodeByIdAsync). To keep code simpler, preload all components into a map at call start:\n```js\nconst COMP={}; for (const [k,id] of Object.entries(IDMAP)) COMP[k]=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\nfunction inst(key,parent,x,y,w,h){const i=COMP[key].createInstance();i.resize(w,h||w);i.x=x;i.y=y;parent.appendChild(i);return i;}\n```\nAll sync then. \n\nButton instance: COMP.btn.createInstance() → resize(327,52); its label \"Continue\" is a child text — for \"Send\" button override child.characters (need font loaded). \n\nNow the build plan per call:\n\n**Call A (setup):** loadFonts; check fonts available; create 11 screen frames (empty, named, positioned, bg); create component section: my reusable components:\n- Tab Bar ×4 (Home/Analytics/Cards/Profile active)\n- Segmented ×3 (03/04/05)\n- IconAction (Send/Receive/Add) ×3\n- TopicChip (selected/default) ×2\n- OTPBox ×1\n- BillCard ×1\n- TxnRow ×1\n- CryptoRow ×1\n- ContactChip (add + person) ×2\n- Key (keypad) ×1\n- IconButtonCircle ×2 (plain, bordered)\n\nWhere components live: same page (03 · Workspace) below at y=950. Fine.\n\nComponent construction functions with absolute positions inside component frames.\n\nTab bar design (375×64 + border): white fill, stroke top? Use drop shadow: {type:'DROP_SHADOW', color rgba(21,21,33,0.04), offset {0,-4}, radius 16}. Items centered: 4 items evenly: each 375/4 = 93.75. Icon 24 centered at item center, y=12; label y=42, Medium 11. Active: deep color; inactive: muted #A5A3B0. \n\nSegmented (335×40): bg #EFEDF8 radius 12; active pill white radius 9, shadow subtle, width (335-8)/3=109, x=4+idx*109, y=4, h=32; label Medium 12.5 ink centered; inactive Medium 12.5 muted. Labels: \"My Balance\", \"Upcoming Bills\", \"Transactions\". Use fontSize 12. Text centered — compute width via auto-resize then center by setting x = segX + (109-w)/2.\n\nIconAction (label under): frame 76×74: circle 48 x=14 y=0 fill primary, icon 22 tinted ink centered (x=14+13, y=13); label Medium 12 ink centered y=56. Names: \"Action / Send\" etc.\n\nBillCard (335×76): white radius 16, padding: logo square 44 at (16,16) bg #F6F5FA radius 12 with logo instance 28 centered (x+8,y+8); name SemiBold 14 at (72,16); meta Regular 11 muted at (72,37): \"Due Sep 05, 2023 · 1 month\"; category Regular 10 sec at (72,54)?? hmm too much text. Layout: left: logo; middle: name (y14), \"Due Sep 05, 2023\" (y36); chips row: cycle chip \"1 month\" + \"Subscriptions\" — place at middle (y55) as text \"1 month · Subscriptions\" Regular 10 muted; right: amount SemiBold 15 at (x right-90, y14, align right); \"Pay now\" button 84×30 radius 15 primary bg, text Medium 11.5 ink centered, at (right-84-16, y36). \nComponent children naming for overrides: name texts \"Name\",\"Meta\",\"Amount\". Logos: nested instance \"Logo\" — swap per usage via logoInst.swapComponent(COMP.logoNetflix).\n\nTxnRow (335×56): white bg? If rows inside a white card, row transparent. Make row component with transparent fill: logo square 40 (16,8) bg #F6F5FA radius 12, lo